Real-World Example
Suppose you are building a Product Management REST API.
Dependency
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
    <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-web</artifactId>
</dependency>
Controller
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/products")
public class ProductController {

    @GetMapping
    public String getProducts() {
        return "Products Retrieved Successfully";
    }
}
Run Application
@SpringBootApplication
public class ProductApplication {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        SpringApplication.run(ProductApplication.class, args);
    }
}
Without configuring Tomcat or Spring MVC manually, the REST API is ready to use.
This is possible because of Auto Configuration.
